WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:06.030
From gigantic, indestructible, self-regenerating
reptiles, to enormous, tentacled, telepathic

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:11.610
organisms, it should come as no surprise that
the SCP Foundation has gone head to head against

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.959
a lot of large-scale aggressors - or LSAs
- in its time.

00:00:15.959 --> 00:00:20.520
Naturally, a creature of heightened size and
aggression can often prove challenging to

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.600
contain, and the threat these LSAs pose is
often far too big to ignore.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.010
But anyone familiar with the Foundation will
tell you, they’re not above using any methods

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:36.129
necessary to keep these creatures contained:
huge vats of molecular acid, impenetrable

00:00:36.129 --> 00:00:40.649
cells, disposable, D-Class personnel, even
other SCPs.

00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:46.460
But what other SCPs could possibly be big
enough, and tough enough, to handle some of

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:49.300
the Foundation’s biggest and baddest?

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:54.760
Meet SCP-5514, otherwise known as “The Dragon
Slayer.”

00:00:54.760 --> 00:01:01.230
While it might sound like something out of
an anime, SCP-5514 is a massive robotic mech

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:05.280
designed to take on the worst other SCPs can
throw at it.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.870
For any who are unfamiliar with the term,
a mech, or mecha, usually refers to an upright-standing

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:14.500
machine or automaton controlled by a human
pilot.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.790
What distinguishes a mech from a vehicle,
is their often-humanoid shape, standing bipedally,

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:22.490
and they are often hundreds of meters tall.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:28.781
All of this is true of SCP-5514, and in fact,
given that it requires a trained member of

00:01:28.781 --> 00:01:34.270
Foundation staff to operate it, the mech itself
requires very little in the way of containment.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:40.509
Only members of Mobile Task Force Eta-5 are
trained and authorized to pilot SCP-5514.

00:01:40.509 --> 00:01:45.770
This is one of the SCP Foundation’s specialized
units, specifically designed to deal with

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:51.390
the threat of Large-Scale Aggressors, much
like SCP-5514 itself.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:56.890
But SCP-5514 wasn’t discovered or captured
by the Foundation to use for the containment

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:03.030
of LSAs, nor was it stolen from a foreign
military or found buried under the ground.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.609
Then, where did it come from?

00:02:05.609 --> 00:02:07.050
And who built it?

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:11.140
Working with the Global Occult Coalition and
the government of Hy-Brasil, an anomalous

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:17.350
island off the west coast of Ireland, the
Foundation themselves constructed SCP-5514,

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:19.930
using various anomalous methods and techniques.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:26.760
In 1988, a Foundation site was destroyed by
an unidentified LSA, highlighting the inadequacy

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:31.430
of the current defenses against these larger,
more damage-resistant creatures.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:37.129
The Foundation, the Coalition, and Hy-Brasil
formed a joint operation, The KEY Project,

00:02:37.129 --> 00:02:44.159
and examined SCP-2406, an automaton ninety-three
meters tall, thought to be created by ancient

00:02:44.159 --> 00:02:45.159
Mekhanites.

00:02:45.159 --> 00:02:49.980
Together, the KEY Project opted to create
their own, similar machine, viewing it as

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:54.650
the best way to defend against further incursions
with Large-Scale Aggressors.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:58.930
The construction of SCP-5514 began in 1990.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:03.459
The intention of all parties involved in the
KEY Project, including the Foundation, was

00:03:03.459 --> 00:03:07.299
that The Dragon Slayer would be deployed in
the event of an attack by an LSA.

00:03:07.299 --> 00:03:12.180
It would arrive at cities under attack and
immediately engage Large-Scale Aggressors

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:13.510
in combat.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:17.040
Building of the mech continued at a consistent
pace for eight years.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:24.550
However, it was the occurrence of SCP-5391,
and subsequent intervention by the O5 Council,

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:29.629
that accelerated the creation of The Dragon
Slayer, by any means necessary.

00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:36.349
On June 30th 1998, a number of seismic disturbances
were detected, including tsunamis, tremors,

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:40.079
and volcanic activity both underwater and
above-ground.

00:03:40.079 --> 00:03:44.220
What followed was the appearance of multiple
Large-Scale Aggressors, which would soon become

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.890
designated as SCP-5391.

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:53.280
The exact kind of scenario that The Dragon
Slayer was being built for had already arrived,

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.739
and the mech was still far from completion.

00:03:55.739 --> 00:04:00.260
While the Foundation and its allies deployed
forces to drive the enormous creatures back

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:07.360
to the oceans, something needed to be done
to bring SCP-5514 into the fight, and fast.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:12.580
The O5 Council authorized the use of anomalous
materials in the continued construction of

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:17.560
The Dragon Slayer, both to speed up the process
and have it ready for deployment, but also

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:24.330
to give the mech every advantage against the
abundance of Large-Scale Aggressors from SCP-5391.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:31.190
As a result, SCP-5514 was designed to incorporate
features and technology far beyond that of

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:34.270
any conventional, military-grade weapons.

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:38.720
The first hurdle: How do you power a machine
the size of SCP-5514?

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:44.410
Naturally, with the most gigantic nuclear
furnace there is… the sun.

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:50.800
More specifically, a perpetually-stable, miniaturized
sun known as SCP-037.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:55.330
Even though it’s only got a diameter of
two inches, this little sucker is better than

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:56.800
premium fuel.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:02.220
The surface temperature of SCP-037 is around
five thousand Kelvin, generating plenty of

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:06.030
energy to power the SCP-5514 mech.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:10.310
Stored in The Dragon Slayer’s chest, this
mini-sun is kept stable by sub-dimensional

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:15.880
portals that vent excess energy off of this
plane of reality, stopping the mech, its pilot,

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.070
and anything around it from melting.

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:24.310
In fact, SCP-037 produces so much juice that
only one percent of its energy output is enough

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:26.120
to fully power SCP-5514.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:29.660
Now, that’s the power source sorted.

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:31.750
But how do you solve the weight problem?

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:37.479
Given the sheer size of SCP-5514, it would
be easy for it to be cumbersome, and potentially

00:05:37.479 --> 00:05:40.830
cause catastrophic collateral damage to its
surrounding area.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:46.480
Well, the mech’s weight is a problem for
somewhere else, a whole other dimension in

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:47.480
fact.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:53.130
Much like the excess heat from its power source,
various heavy portions of the SCP-5514 mech

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:56.099
have had their weight shunted off to a tiny
pocket dimension.

00:05:56.099 --> 00:06:01.289
It was ensured, during the creation of the
mech, that this alteration was perfectly calculated

00:06:01.289 --> 00:06:07.410
so that SCP-5514 wouldn’t lose any mass
or density, so it operates as if it were only

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:09.729
a fraction of its actual weight.

00:06:09.729 --> 00:06:12.729
Of course, being weightless makes flight a
whole lot easier.

00:06:12.729 --> 00:06:15.669
Oh did we forget to mention that?

00:06:15.669 --> 00:06:18.259
SCP-5514 can fly as well.

00:06:18.259 --> 00:06:22.240
This “feature” actually became a part
of the mech completely by accident during

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:27.919
the construction of SCP-5514, when an attempt
to regulate the mech’s internal circulation

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:31.490
of air led to it having its own gravity field.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:37.530
This allowed SCP-5514 to fly, without the
aid of any turbines or other means.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:42.440
While this was an unintentional mistake, no
attempt has ever been made to correct it,

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:47.560
for fear that could lead to SCP-5514 being
grounded permanently.

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:52.960
Naturally, going up against creatures so large
that they require their own sub-category means

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:57.039
that SCP-5514 needs an equally-formidable
arsenal.

00:06:57.039 --> 00:06:59.720
So, let’s move on to talk weaponry.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:05.070
Mounted on the mech’s shoulder is a Beowulf-Sigurd
Railgun, an anomalous weapon that also doesn’t

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:07.259
obey the laws of physics at all.

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:12.240
The Beowulf-Sigurd uses altered gravity to
affect the weight of its targets, causing

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:15.090
projectiles to impact with higher velocity.

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:18.970
Even the thickest-skinned LSAs wouldn’t
want to be staring down the barrel end of

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:20.389
one of those.

00:07:20.389 --> 00:07:25.870
Big guns aside, the SCP-5514 mech also wields
a Cold Iron Sword.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:30.550
Over sixty-five feet long, this weapon was
contributed to The Dragon Slayer by the Hy-Brasil

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:34.940
Royal Court, members of the collaborative
KEY Project that created the mech.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:39.449
Sure, a Large-Scale Aggressor with thicker
hide might take a few extra swings to draw

00:07:39.449 --> 00:07:44.840
blood, but it will feel those swings for a
long time after, since any wounds inflicted

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:48.160
by the Cold Iron Sword will not regenerate.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:54.210
Serving as less of an offensive weapon, the
SCP-5514 mech also features a unique armament

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:56.840
known as the Thousand Word Arrows.

00:07:56.840 --> 00:08:01.180
As pretentious as it might sound, within the
mech are seven poets.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:05.909
Their role is to write and recite poems that
detail the slaying of monsters, and these

00:08:05.909 --> 00:08:09.280
recitals are then broadcast from The Dragon
Slayer.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:13.092
On the surface, this seems to have no practical
applications during a fight with LSAs, however,

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:18.820
the goal of the Thousand Word Arrows is a
form of psychological warfare.

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:23.419
The recital of poems telling of the mech’s
victory and the defeat of Large-Scale Aggressors

00:08:23.419 --> 00:08:29.840
is intended to have the effect of demoralizing
SCP-5514’s adversaries, while encouraging

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:31.550
the pilot during combat.

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:38.050
Additionally, worn atop the head of the SCP-5514
mech, almost like a hat, is a discus with

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:39.960
plasma-coated edges.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:44.420
If The Dragon Slayer needs to deal damage
at range, then it can hurl this disc and recall

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:47.650
it immediately thanks to built-in electromagnets.

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:54.590
In emergency scenarios, if the Cold Iron Sword
is damaged or dropped and irretrievable, SCP-5514

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:57.630
is also equipped with an additional melee
weapon.

00:08:57.630 --> 00:09:01.420
Stored in the right arm of the mech is a Holdout
Plasma Wristblade.

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:05.180
This superheated blade is strong enough to
cut through almost anything.

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:09.220
However, this blade is strictly to be used
as a backup weapon.

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:16.570
Finally, should all else fail, one of SCP-5514’s
greatest strengths can also be used as a deadly

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:17.570
weapon.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:23.080
The Emergency Sun Vent allows a fraction of
the excessive power from SCP-037 to be released,

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:29.760
at the risk of causing massive damage, not
only to LSAs, but also any civilians or structures

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:30.760
nearby.

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:35.170
It is because of the destructive risk involved,
that this weapon is only authorized to be

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:37.020
used as a final resort.

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:42.150
And luckily, SCP-5514 is currently undefeated.

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:49.200
Since the arrival of multiple Large-Scale
Aggressors as a result of SCP-5391, the SCP-5514

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:54.730
mech has managed to successfully eliminate
twelve of these LSA creatures, either by terminating

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:57.610
or otherwise incapacitating them.

00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:03.360
Given that its completion was fast-tracked
through the use of anomalous elements, SCP-5514’s

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:08.270
first combat deployments also served as field
tests of the mech’s operation and its various

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:10.340
weapons and features.

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:17.010
Arriving in Tokyo overseen by the Foundation’s
own Captain Rosales and Dr. Kaori, SCP-5514’s

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:23.480
first target was a creature designated LSA-Wake-02,
as well as several other unidentified large

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:24.480
creatures.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:31.140
As the LSA was about to attack Tokyo Harbor,
SCP-5514 was dispatched, its arrival heralded

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:33.240
by the Thousand Word Arrows.

00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:34.240
“Champion!

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:35.240
Champion!

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:39.390
Exalt in the glory of the Dragon Slayer!”
the poets recited.

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:41.320
Surprisingly, the poetry worked.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:47.210
Hearing it had a noticeable effect on LSA-Wake-02,
causing the creature to back away shrieking.

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:54.380
With a single throw of the Rounded Recoiling
Plasma, SCP-5514 immediately beheaded Wake-02,

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:59.710
damaging a number of the other nearby LSAs
as it retrieved the disk via its electromagnets.

00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:03.770
Once again, the Thousand Word Arrows cheered
on the mech and its pilot, reciting “The

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:05.660
vicious beast’s slain!

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:08.130
Gone to those which were once bane!”

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:14.090
After dispatching several of the minor LSAs
with its Cold Iron Sword, SCP-5514 became

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:17.600
aware that Wake-02 was not fully down for
the count.

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:22.050
A second head had protruded from the mouth
of the creature’s first, issuing some sort

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:25.640
of retreat call to the remaining LSAs in Tokyo
Harbor.

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:31.490
This second head then shot towards SCP-5514,
narrowly missing its leg, but allowing another

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:34.240
LSA to close the distance and prepare an attack.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:39.070
Luckily, the SCP-5514 mech’s sword cleaved
the beast in two.

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:44.250
The mech began firing on the remains of Wake-02
with its Beowulf-Sigurd Railgun, launching

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:48.280
itself into the air and flying towards the
target while bringing its Cold Iron Sword

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:49.950
down through the air.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:56.470
With a single motion, SCP-5514 brought the
blade all the way down the LSAs body, from

00:11:56.470 --> 00:12:01.950
the creature’s head to its caudal fin, gutting
the Large-Scale Aggressor and splitting its

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.930
entire body in two.

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:08.680
After one final squirm, both halves were finally
still.

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:12.160
SCP-5514 had passed its first field test.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:17.530
The mech functioned exactly as designed, all
its various weapons and features working in

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:22.660
tandem to defeat a creature far too large
and powerful for any conventional force to

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:23.660
handle.

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:25.400
“And thus, the deed was done!

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:26.400
Exalt!

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:27.400
Exalt!

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:31.520
In the glory of the Dragon Slayer!” the
Thousand Word Arrows called out as the other

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.180
LSAs retreated.

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:38.090
One can’t help but feel cautiously optimistic
about our chances of survival knowing that

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:44.440
the Foundation has SCP-5514 as the first line
of defence against huge, monstrous beings

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:46.410
that threaten humanity.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:54.230
As the situation with SCP-5391 continues,
the SCP-5514 mech remains on the front line,

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:59.770
standing between innocent human beings and
the looming shapes of multiple Large-Scale

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:00.770
Aggressors.

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:05.070
With creatures that pose such a large-scale
threat, it certainly is lucky that disparate

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:10.350
groups were able to put aside their differences
and work together to build a large-scale mech,

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:15.340
and because they did, now we have The Dragon
Slayer on our side.

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:22.020
Now check out “SCP-5545 - Mysterious Tunnels
In Antarctica - Abnormality” and “SCP

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:26.930
Chaos Insurgency Explained” for more incredible
stories from the SCP Foundation!

